{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/tbl-knot-operator-basis-table-table2-data","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Table","doco:Table"],"label":"tbl:knot-operator-basis-table-table2-data","kind":"table","title":"Data table 2 from rem:knot-operator-basis-table","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-knot-operator-basis-table"],"tags":["extracted-table"],"text":"knot-operator-basis-table-table2-data.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"tbl:knot-operator-basis-table-table2-data\"></a><p><strong>Table 2.</strong> Action of the electron operator\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta(T_{2,2}^{(3)}) = e^- = \\sigma_0\\sigma_1\\sigma_0</code>, whose closure\nin <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">B_3</code> is the Hopf link, on NF basis pairs. Each cell gives the coefficient of the column NF basis\noperator in the product <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i \\cdot e^- \\cdot b_j</code>, exact in the Hecke\namplitude <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h = q - q^{-1}</code>. The six NF basis elements\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{\\ \\gamma,\\ \\sigma_0,\\ \\sigma_1,\\ L_+,\\ L_-,\\ e^-\\ \\}</code>, the\namplitude <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code> and the operator names <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{2,n}^{(3)}</code> are introduced in\nthe parent remark\n<a href=\"#rem:knot-operator-basis-table\" data-at=\"appendix-knot-periodic-table/hecke-operations\">Knot operator action on NF basis pairs</a>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b_i \\cdot e^- \\cdot b_j</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_-</code></th>\n<th align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma \\cdot e^- \\cdot \\gamma</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_0 \\cdot e^- \\cdot \\sigma_1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^2+1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_1 \\cdot e^- \\cdot \\sigma_0</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">—</td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^2+1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gamma \\cdot e^- \\cdot e^-</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^3+h</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^- \\cdot e^- \\cdot \\gamma</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">1</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^3+h</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"left\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^- \\cdot e^- \\cdot e^-</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^3+h</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^4+h^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">h^4+h^2</code></td>\n<td align=\"center\">...</td>\n<td align=\"center\">...</td>\n<td align=\"center\">...</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The elided entries (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\ldots</code>) in the final row are the remaining NF\ncoefficients of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^- \\cdot e^- \\cdot e^-</code> (<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_+</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_-</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">e^-</code>\nchannels); their full symbolic values are recorded in the computation\nattached to the parent\nremark <a href=\"#rem:knot-operator-basis-table\" data-at=\"appendix-knot-periodic-table/hecke-operations\">Knot operator action on NF basis pairs</a>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-knot-periodic-table/knot-operator-basis-table-table2-data.md","heading":"Table","page":"b/tbl-knot-operator-basis-table-table2-data","qa":{"counts":{"pass":43,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":15,"unknown":0,"stale":57}}}
